In Java 8, Function is a functional interface; it takes an argument (object of type T) and returns an object (object of type R). The argument and output can be a different type.

or

Takes one argument of any type and returns a value of same/any type
Essentially , it represents a function that transforms an input of type into an output of type


Function.java

@FunctionalInterface
public interface Function<T, R> {

      R apply(T t);

}

T – Type of the input to the function.
R – Type of the result of the function.


second method(andThen):fun1->fun2
third method(compose):fun2->fun1
fourth method-static(identity):where function is required but no changes should be applied